   522	### 5.6 The minimal compute change for OPEN[FULL-BASIS-TIMEOUT]
   523	
   524	Three, in increasing cost, all standard and none yet in the engine:
   525	
   526	1. **Modular Gröbner + rational reconstruction + exact char-0 verification of
   527	   the cofactors.** Today a "kill" over Q means running `std` over Q for
   528	   1800 s. Instead: run `std` mod `p` (seconds), extract the representation
   529	   `1 = Σ hᵢ gᵢ` mod `p` (`lift`), rationally reconstruct the `hᵢ`, then
   530	   **verify `Σ hᵢ gᵢ = 1` exactly over Q by polynomial arithmetic**. The
   531	   verification is a multiplication, not a Gröbner basis: milliseconds. A
   532	   successful lift is a complete char-0 certificate; a failed lift costs one
   533	   more prime. This is the single highest-leverage engineering change and it
   534	   removes the "modular ≠ char 0" caveat that has qualified a dozen results.
