   563	## 5. The pole rows and the Jacobian rows
   564	
   565	**Pole rows** are sec 4.1(1); necessity rests on the branch datum only. Engine
   566	labels: `delta = 2` uses `F: -80,-79,-78` then `-77-k`, `G: -53,-52,-51` then
   567	`-50-k`; `delta = 5/2` uses `F: -187,-185,-183` then `-181-2k`,
   568	`G: -124,-122,-120` then `-118-2k`. The parity in the second branch (because
   569	`t = s^2`) is why the `G` pole rows meet the Jacobian band every second stage
   570	there but every stage at `delta = 2` -- the whole four-stage gap between the two
   571	deaths.
   572	
   573	**Jacobian rows.** `J(F,G) = 1` is an identity in `k[x,y]`, so every coefficient
   574	`[x^i y^j](F_xG_y - F_yG_x)` with `i+j > 0` vanishes and the constant coefficient
   575	is 1. The engine uses only the former, in total degrees `163 = 99+66-2` downward:
   576	
   577	* degree 163 vanishes structurally, not as a row: `J(P^9,P^6) = 54P^{13}J(P,P) = 0`;
   578	* the charged prefix uses `[x^{145}y^{17}]J, ..., [x^{136}y^{26}]J` (degree 162);
   579	* stage 0 adds `[x^{135}y^{27}]J`; stage 1 the remaining degree-162 coefficients
   580	  (`y`-powers 28..162); stage `n >= 2` **all** coefficients of total degree
   581	  `163-n`. Stage 8 imposes all 156 coefficients of degree 155.
   582	
   583	Homogenised, `J(F,G) = x^{163}KJ(1/x, y/x)` with
   584	
   585	```text
   586	KJ = 99 KF (KG)_w - t (KF)_t (KG)_w - 66 (KF)_w KG + (KF)_w t (KG)_t,
   587	```
   588	
   589	so `[x^i y^j]J = [t^{163-i-j} w^j]KJ`: Jacobian total degree `163-n` is `t`-power
   590	`n`, and the label index `k` is the `w`-power (the invariant
   591	`deg_w KJ_n <= 163-n`, i.e. `i >= 0`, is asserted on every run).
   592	
   593	**Well-definedness.** Each `[x^iy^j]J` is `Z`-bilinear in the coefficients of `F`
   594	and `G`, which by Prop 1.2 are polynomials with integer coefficients in the 7161
   595	chart coordinates. So each Jacobian row is such a polynomial and involves **no
   596	branch parameter**: `u,v,rho,c` occur only in the pole and leader rows, and the
   597	Jacobian rows are identical in the two branches. The constant `1` (or a free
   598	`kappa`) lives only in degree 0 and is never touched by `J162...J155`, so no kill
   599	inverts or fixes a Jacobian constant.
   600	
   601	**Mechanism.** Below the `A2/A3/B2` onset, with `A = K2`, `B = K_{B1}`,
   602	`KJ = tA^3(99 A B_w - 96 B A_w) + 3t^2 A^3 (A_w B_t - A_t B_w)`; once
   603	`B_0 = ... = B_{n-2} = 0` have been eliminated,
   604	`[t^n]KJ = A_0^3(99A_0 B_{n-1,w} - (99-3n)B_{n-1}A_{0,w})` with
   605	`A_0 = w^9(w-1)^{24}`. Writing `B_{n-1} = sum_q B1c_{n-1,q}(w-1)^q` and
   606	`A_{0,w} = w^8(w-1)^{23}(33w-9)`,
