    99	## 2. The type-correct statement
   100	
   101	### 2.1 Partition convention
   102	
   103	Fix a multiplicity vector
   104	
   105	```text
   106	lambda = (m_1,...,m_r),       m_i >= 1,       sum_i m_i = u_s,
   107	```
   108	
   109	and distinct packet centres `c_1,...,c_r`.  Then
   110	
   111	```text
   112	p(pi)     = product_i (pi-c_i)^(m_i),
   113	p_red(pi) = product_i (pi-c_i).
   114	```
   115	
   116	A genuine split means `r >= 2`, equivalently the multiplicity partition is not
   117	the one-part partition `[u_s]`.  The phrase in the task
   118	`partition != [1,1,...]` is not equivalent: read literally, it excludes the
   119	fully simple splits `[1,1]` and `[1,1,1]` used in two flagship branches while
   120	still allowing the unsplit partition `[u_s]`.  This report uses the source
   121	definition: at least two distinct roots.
   122	
   123	There is a second small but important point.  Since `p_red` is squarefree by
   124	definition, its discriminant is nonzero after one has specialized to actual
   125	distinct roots over Xu's coefficient field.  Even for an unsplit power,
   126	`p_red` is linear and its conventional discriminant is `1`.  Thus the genuine
   127	condition is
   128	
   129	```text
   130	deg(p_red) = r >= 2       and       disc(p_red) != 0,
   131	```
   132	
   133	not discriminant nonvanishing alone.  This is why `u_s=1` must be excluded
   134	explicitly.
   135	
   136	### 2.2 The fixed-stratum root ring
   137	
   138	An ideal-membership assertion needs a parameter ring, not a single specialized
   139	field point.  Work first on the ordered-root cover of a fixed multiplicity
   140	stratum, with coefficient/tower/jet parameters collectively denoted `theta`:
   141	
   142	```text
   143	A_lambda = k[theta,c_1,...,c_r] / (the fixed chart relations),
   144	R_lambda = disc(p_red)
   145	         = product_{i<j}(c_i-c_j)^2                 (p_red monic).
   146	```
   147	
   148	The expression is symmetric and can subsequently descend through the relevant
   149	root-permutation action.  This stratumwise construction matters: taking the
   150	squarefree part by a gcd is not a polynomial operation on one coefficient
   151	space across loci where multiplicities jump.  One must either use the root
   152	cover above or a coefficient/subresultant chart with the appropriate
   153	subresultants inverted.
   154	
   155	Let `I_lambda` be the ideal generated by all *proved necessary* rows in that
   156	same ring before the genuine-split localization.  The genuine part of the
   157	necessary chart is, with `V_A` and `D_A` denoting subsets of
   158	`Spec(A_lambda)`,
   159	
   160	```text
   161	X_lambda^gen = V_A(I_lambda) intersect D_A(R_lambda).
   162	```
   163	
   164	### 2.3 Fixed-stratum localization theorem
   165	
   166	**Theorem 2.1 (exact algebraic criterion).**  For any commutative ring
   167	`A_lambda`, ideal `I_lambda`, and element `R_lambda`, the following are
   168	equivalent:
   169	
   170	1. `V_A(I_lambda) intersect D_A(R_lambda)` is empty in `Spec(A_lambda)`;
   171	2. `I_lambda A_lambda[R_lambda^(-1)] = A_lambda[R_lambda^(-1)]`;
   172	3. `R_lambda` belongs to `radical(I_lambda)`;
   173	4. `R_lambda^N` belongs to `I_lambda` for some integer `N >= 0`.
   174	
   175	*Proof.*  The first and third statements are the standard
   176	`V_A(I) subset V_A(R)` equivalence.  If `R^N` is in `I`, it becomes a unit after
   177	localization, proving the second statement.  Conversely, writing `1` as a
   178	finite combination of localized generators and clearing denominators gives a
   179	power of `R` in `I`.  The case `N=0` is exactly `I=(1)`.  QED.
   180	
   181	This is the rigorous content behind a discriminant kill.  Exact membership
   182	`R in I` is the stronger kill-order-one case, not the general criterion.
   183	Likewise, “the chart dies iff `R` is a unit” is not the right formulation:
   184	`R` is a unit in `A[R^(-1)]` by construction, whether or not the localized
   185	ideal is proper.  At an individual genuine field-valued datum, `R` is already
   186	a nonzero scalar.  The nontrivial assertion is `R in radical(I)` in the
   187	unlocalized family ring.
   188	
   189	Consequently, **if** the missing assertion
   190	`R_lambda in radical(I_lambda)` were proved for every admissible genuine split
   191	datum, then MINOR-EMPTY would indeed be unconditional on the genuine split
   192	stratum: `R_lambda != 0` is part of that stratum.  The automatic nonvanishing
   193	does not prove the radical containment.
